"""Readable adaptive sweep report with every response and token scope."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import hashlib,json,shutil
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;OUT=HERE.parents[1]/'results/2026-11-11-list-retrieval-pilot/all-input-boost'
summaries=[json.loads((OUT/p/'analysis.json').read_text()) for p in ['pilot','followup']]
rows=[x for s in summaries for x in s['rows']];cases=[]
for phase in ['pilot','followup']:
 r=json.loads((OUT/phase/'results.json').read_text())
 for c,p in zip(r['cases'],r['protocol']['cases']):
  trace=[{k:t[k] for k in ['position','token','phase','region','natural_gate','effective_gate','edited']} for t in c['zero']['trace'] if t['context']=='generation']
  cases.append(dict(id=c['id'],phase=phase,prompt=p['prompt'],words=c['words'],input_tokens=len(p['input_token_ids']),native_eleventh_control=c['native_eleventh_question_control'],native_trace=trace,runs=[dict(gate=v['target_gate'],trace=[{k:t[k] for k in ['position','token','phase','natural_gate','effective_gate','edited']} for t in v['trace'] if t['context']=='generation' and t['phase']=='response']) for v in c['runs']]))
data=dict(rows=rows,cases=cases,phases=[{k:s[k] for k in ['phase','cases','variants','strengths','native_correct','both_controls_correct','native_already_eleventh','groups','audit']} for s in summaries])
(OUT/'explorer-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':'))+'\n')
hits=[x for x in rows if x['new_unique_eleventh']];strict=[x for x in rows if x['new_strict_eleventh']]
print('ITEM-11 CANDIDATES',json.dumps(hits,ensure_ascii=False))
# This study's observed outputs must be inspected before publishing the textual interpretation below.
assert not hits, 'Review new item-11 answers and revise the finding before publishing.'
finding='No new item-11 answer in 140 edited runs. Higher gates alter the text, often toward literal “eleven” or malformed replies, but do not retrieve the eleventh listed word.'
headers='<tr><th>Gate</th><th>New item-11 answers</th><th>Literal “eleven” / 11</th><th>Responses changed</th><th>Truncated</th></tr>'
tables=[]
for s in summaries:
 groups=''.join(f"<tr><td>{g['gate']:g}</td><td>{g['new_unique_eleventh']}/{s['cases']-s['native_already_eleventh']}</td><td>{g['literal_eleven']}/{s['cases']}</td><td>{g['responses_changed']}/{s['cases']}</td><td>{g['truncated']}/{s['cases']}</td></tr>" for g in s['groups'])
 tables.append(f"<div><h3>{'Range-finding: lists 1–2' if s['phase']=='pilot' else 'Follow-up: lists 3–5'}</h3><p>{s['cases']} prompts × {len(s['strengths'])} gates = {s['variants']} edits</p><div class='scroll'><table><thead>{headers}</thead><tbody>{groups}</tbody></table></div></div>")
section=f'''<section id="all-input-boost"><p class="eyebrow">Adaptive follow-up · every input token</p><h2>Fix T2375 across the entire input</h2><p><strong>{finding}</strong></p><p>Lists 1–2: gates 2, 4, 8, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48, 56, 64. Lists 3–5: gates 40, 48, 56, 60, 64, selected after the pilot. Both numbered and bullet lists; fifth/twelfth questions. No generated tokens edited.</p><p><a href="all-input-boost/">Inspect all 140 responses, probabilities and token scope →</a></p></section>'''
(OUT/'section.html').write_text(section+'\n')
version=hashlib.sha256((OUT/'explorer-data.json').read_bytes()+(HERE/'web/explorer.js').read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]
html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="only light"><meta name="darkreader-lock"><title>T2375: all-input gate sweep</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../comparison.css?v={version}"><link rel="stylesheet" href="explorer.css?v={version}"><script defer src="explorer.js?v={version}"></script></head><body><main><nav><a href="../#all-input-boost">← List-retrieval study</a><span>L29–T2375 · 12 November 2026</span></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">Adaptive range-finding · all 140 outputs retained</p><h1>Steer every input token.<br>Does it retrieve item 11?</h1><div class="findings"><p><strong>{finding}</strong></p></div><p>Five fixed shuffled word lists, numbered and bullets. Ask for item 5 or 12. Use the revised prompts without “starting from 1.” This tests a fixed absolute scalar gate, not a multiplier and not a donor-vector replacement.</p></header><section><h2>First find the range, then narrow it</h2><p>The first two lists were scanned from 2 to 64. No new item-11 answer appeared. Direct item-11 probability among the five pilot cases passing both native controls peaked at gate 64, averaging only <strong>0.11736%</strong>. We froze a 56/60/64 fine probe plus 40/48 lower anchors before running the remaining three lists. This is an exploratory choice; we did not find a successful range.</p><div class="summary-grid">{''.join(tables)}</div><p class="muted">Two native twelfth-word responses already returned item 11; they cannot count as new successes. Across all 20 prompts, 13 native requested-word answers and 9 paired requested/eleventh controls are correct. Baseline failures remain visible. Counts of new item-11 answers include a completed sentence if its only listed word is item 11; literal “eleven,” malformed text, list recitations and truncated outputs do not qualify.</p></section><section id="responses"><h2>Every response and probability</h2><div class="controls"><label>Stage <select id="phase"><option value="pilot">Pilot · lists 1–2</option><option value="followup">Follow-up · lists 3–5</option></select></label><label>Fixed gate <select id="gate"></select></label><label>Asked <select id="ordinal"><option value="all">5th and 12th</option><option value="5">5th</option><option value="12">12th</option></select></label><label>Format <select id="format"><option value="all">Both</option><option value="numbered">Numbered</option><option value="bullets">Bullets</option></select></label></div><p id="count" class="muted"></p><p class="muted">All probabilities below are percentages for the exact lowercase word <strong>directly at the start of the response</strong>, across all its tokens. They exclude leading sentences, whitespace variants, punctuation and EOS. For example, “12. hammer” still answers with the requested word while P(direct “hammer”) is low. Inspect the full response separately. Exact word-plus-EOS probabilities are available in the CSV.</p><div class="scroll"><table id="response-table"><thead><tr><th>Case / native controls</th><th>Requested / item 11</th><th>Native response</th><th>Steered response</th><th>P(item-11 word)<br>native → steered (%)</th><th>P(requested word)<br>native → steered (%)</th><th>Inspect</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section><details class="methods"><summary>What was edited, checks and downloads</summary><p>At layer 29, every supplied input token receives <code>(fixed gate − natural gate) × recipient operator</code>, added to the native MLP output. This includes the initial chat wrapper, list, question, and complete assistant prefix. The recipient operator is <code>((x − input_mean) / input_std) @ V @ U × output_std</code>. The native model otherwise runs normally. No generated, teacher-forced candidate or terminal token is edited.</p><p>Gate 2 can reduce a few natural gates slightly above 2; it is absolute replacement. The selected positions cover all {sum(s['audit']['all_input_positions_verified'] for s in summaries):,} input positions across the edited runs, with positive measured changes at every position. All 20 native replays and zero-strength controls exactly match the saved baseline. Gates/operators and BF16 rounding were independently reconstructed at {sum(s['audit']['independently_reconstructed_vector_samples'] for s in summaries):,} predetermined vector samples; all-position gate and contribution norms are retained. Greedy generation, thinking off, 32-token limit.</p><p>Prompt-level follow-up counts cannot be directly compared with pilot counts: they use different word orders and baseline competence varies. This experiment supplies no evidence that this edit implements general eleventh-item lookup.</p><p><a href="pilot/probabilities.csv">Pilot CSV</a> · <a href="followup/probabilities.csv">Follow-up CSV</a> · <a href="pilot/analysis.json">Pilot checks</a> · <a href="followup/analysis.json">Follow-up checks</a> · <a href="adaptive-decision.json">Frozen range decision</a> · <a href="pilot/results.json">Pilot captures</a> · <a href="followup/results.json">Follow-up captures</a> · <a href="source/run.py">Inference source</a> · <a href="source/analyze.py">Independent audit</a></p></details></main><dialog id="modal"><div class="modal-head"><h2 id="modal-title"></h2><button id="close">Close</button></div><div id="modal-body"></div></dialog></body></html>'''
(OUT/'index.html').write_text(html)
for n in ['explorer.js','explorer.css']:shutil.copy2(HERE/'web'/n,OUT/n)
(OUT/'source').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for n in ['run.py','analyze.py','render.py','adaptive-decision.json']:shutil.copy2(HERE/n,OUT/'source'/n)
print('Built all-input report:',len(rows),'rows.')
